# Favalog environment variables (example).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and must NEVER be committed. This example contains variable NAMES
# ONLY — no real secrets.
#
# The existing frontend runs entirely on mock data and does NOT require any of
# these to build or run. They become relevant only for the authentication /
# onboarding surfaces (sign in, sign up, password reset, onboarding). With none
# of these set, public mock browsing keeps working and the auth entry points
# present a controlled "accounts aren't available yet" state.

# --- Public Supabase configuration (safe to expose to the browser) ----------
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are ever sent to the client. For local development
# these come from `npx supabase status` after `npm run supabase:start`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase's current key terminology: the *publishable* key (formerly "anon").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Public site URL (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin used to build absolute auth callback/email links when the
# request origin is unavailable. On Vercel this is derived automatically; set it
# explicitly for a custom domain. Must be a full origin, e.g. https://app.example.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --- Google OAuth toggle (public, NOT a secret) -----------------------------
# Set to "true" only when Google is configured in the Supabase dashboard
# (Authentication → Providers → Google). This flag merely decides whether the
# "Continue with Google" button is shown; the Google client id/secret live in
# the Supabase dashboard and are NEVER placed here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_GOOGLE_ENABLED=true

# --- Server-only secret (NEVER exposed to the browser) ----------------------
# The secret (service-role) key bypasses Row Level Security and is intended for
# trusted server-side administrative processes only (e.g. future catalog
# ingestion). It is NOT required for normal application startup or for the
# auth/onboarding flows. Do not prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never read it
# from client code.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- AI Discovery: catalog search (server-only) -----------------------------
# OpenAI API key used ONLY server-side to embed the search query for the
# semantic half of hybrid catalog search. It is a SECRET: never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never read it from client code, and it is never logged or placed
# in an error. It is NOT required to build or run: with no key, catalog search
# runs keyword-only (Postgres full-text search) and the page still works.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Kill switch for the semantic (pgvector) half of catalog search. Defaults to
# ENABLED when unset. Set to a falsey token (e.g. "false" or "0") to disable
# semantic search; keyword search keeps working either way. Server-only — do not
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# SEMANTIC_SEARCH_ENABLED=true

# --- External Providers: catalog ingestion (server-only) --------------------
# TMDB API Read Access Token (v4 auth). Used ONLY server-side to search and
# import movies and TV shows. It is a SECRET: never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never read it from client code, and it is never logged.
# Not required to build or run. TMDB attribution is required before any
# user-facing results are enabled.
# TMDB_API_READ_TOKEN=

# Contact email for Open Library API identification. Used in the User-Agent
# string (`Favalog/<version> (<email>)`) to help Open Library identify our
# traffic. Live book requests fail closed if this is missing. No personal
# info should be hardcoded in the repository. Not required to build or run.
# OPEN_LIBRARY_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# Kill switch for federated external Explore discovery (Catalog Platform v1B):
# searching TMDB / Open Library from /explore and offering an on-demand import.
# Defaults to OFF (opt-in): external discovery runs ONLY when this is a truthy
# token (true/1/on/yes) AND the relevant provider above is configured. When
# unset/disabled or a provider is unconfigured, /explore keeps its existing
# local hybrid search unchanged (no external calls, no build/import-time crash).
# Server-only — do not prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# EXTERNAL_CATALOG_ENABLED=false
